        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add privacy primer]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44877</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44877"/>
        <updated>2026-07-23T22:27:36.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This is a "privacy primer" guide, based on the outline in <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PqupzU-IbqZqOBoNa32KncrbnApxhMZY6WHYFRl2MQM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.cdq8kssa3b0a" rel="nofollow">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PqupzU-IbqZqOBoNa32KncrbnApxhMZY6WHYFRl2MQM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.cdq8kssa3b0a</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">It's supposed to be a kind of introduction to privacy for web developers, with most of the principles taken from <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/privacy-principles/" rel="nofollow">https://www.w3.org/TR/privacy-principles/</a>, although I've tried to make it a bit more accessible than that.</p>
<p dir="auto">I've also tried to integrate some of the content from <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Privacy" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Privacy</a> - I feel like this page ought to replace that one, so we should integrate everything we think is needed from there.</p>
<p dir="auto">I think this also overlaps with the "designing for privacy" page in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4942910853" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44876" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/44876/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44876">#44876</a>, so it would be good if we can to integrate anything extra from that page into here.</p>]]></content>
